            "notes": "Pick up zip grease for sniping. Keep whatever greens you can afford.\n\nImportant playstyle notes: Be very mindful of concussion mine usage. The vast majority of mines should not be used for damage alone.\n1) This is your setup; don't use mine unless you plan to snipe with the next 2 shots. It's preferable to just not use a mine if you are going to shoot shields.\n2) It's encouraged to take long range duels. Do NOT start the duel without zip grease activated. If that means wasting a mine around a corner before peaking, so be it.\n\nFiner point: your job is primarily to stay out of the brawl, and only peak ranged heroes when taking on a duel. Look for off angles with exposed squishies. While on those off angles between duels you can help your tank in the following ways:\n1) DON'T continuously shoot the tank. This just focuses all healing to the tank, gives value to heal tank builds,  and lets enemy dps have free positioning.\n2) Instead, occasionally do a burst of damage on the tank for 1 or 2 sets of zip grease combos. This works BECAUSE you are on an off angle and the tank isn't shielding directed at you. The goal isn't to directly kill the tank unless they are already low, instead it is to bring support focus back to them.\n3) Consider the tank matchup and use mine for displacement of the enemy tank to your team's advantage, when doing a tank burst.",
