            "created_at": "2025-08-26T02:55:45.089747+00:00",
            "notes": "Time for a build shift!\nNow we want to empower zip grease shots with AP rather than WP. We should have enough money to pick up:\n    Mark of the Kitsune\n    Three Tap Tommy Gun\n\nThis gives similar damage (maybe even higher) to zip grease shots, but now mines and tire are more impactful. For those times when you turn to apply a tank burst, the mine AOE might also get those nearby. Keep off angle sniping though. Those solo picks are what open up fights.\n\nPower: I usually pick up Double Trouble (2x traps) for 2 reasons.\n      1) Often the front line could use a bit of help. Place traps early and often along pathing lines where they will not likely be destroyed by accident. In the ebb and flow of tank battles, the enemy will often step in them.\n      2) As sniper rat you WILL be hard targeted. Every game is different, but traps can cover flank routes (or be flank bait) and slow down enemy pathing to you so there is more time for mine cooldowns to reset.\n\nAlternate power: \n    Bingo is always a good backup if traps aren't getting value. \n    Slapnel might be good vs DVa where it is difficult to mine jump away as she DMs the mine.",
